Solves #5284

The underlying issue here, the one being addressed, is that httpUrl, exactly as it currently stands right now, ends up allowing a single slash (as in the case of http:/example.com), and it likewise also goes and allows no slash at all whatsoever (as in the case of http:example.com)

example :
{
"parsedUser": {
"website": "http:example.com"
}
}

{
"parsedUser": {
"website": "https:/[www.google.com]
}
}

The fix that is being made for this whole thing is to go right ahead and add in a strict protocol:// check, and then to go and place that particular check specifically before the call that ends up being made to new URL(), doing so over inside of the httpUrl() function its very own self

